   "thesis": "Bidding is open until 23 Nov and was 0.48x subscribed on day 2; QIBs are at 1.37x while retail is 0.24x. Institutions usually bid late, so early numbers say little. The issue is entirely offer-for-sale, so no money goes to the company. One lot costs about Rs 14,960; only a small bet is sensible, ideally after checking final-day demand.",
   "analysis": {
    "score": 30,
    "verdict": "Avoid",
    "reasons": [
     "Subscription: QIB 3.94x*0.5, NII 0.60x*0.3, RETAIL 0.41x*0.2 -> weighted 2.23x.",
     "Score 30 is below 40: demand is weak for the size."
    ],
    "risks": [
     "Offer-for-sale heavy: 100% of the issue (Rs 9,001 cr of Rs 9,001 cr) pays existing holders, not the company.",
     "No matching DRHP found in SEBI's recent listing (older filings are not searched)."
    ],
    "listing_view": {
     "low_pct": -5,
     "high_pct": 8,
     "basis": "QIB 3.94x*0.5, NII 0.60x*0.3, RETAIL 0.41x*0.2 -> weighted 2.23x. Rule of thumb for this multiple on a Mainboard issue, not a forecast"
    },
    "listing_px": [
     129.2,
